# Screening: cut-v9 (director release `screen-cut-v9`, editor a424f83), 10:58

## How I watched (read this first)
I am a model, not a person with ears and a screen. I could not play the film in real time or hear it, and I could not turn the subtitles on or off in a browser.
- **Picture:** I looked at a frame every 3 s over the whole 10:58 (220 frames in 11 sheets), at 0.5 s steps for 0:22-0:32 and for 7:08-7:16, and at 1 s steps over the credits start. I also measured how much each shot changes from frame to frame (ffmpeg, 4 fps) as a rough stand-in for how much moves. I did not see motion as motion; jumps shorter than 3 s can hide between my frames.
- **Sound:** I transcribed all the audio with Whisper (small) and also re-checked every one of the 75 subtitle cues against the audio in a window around it. I measured loudness, silence and black frames with ffmpeg. This tells me what words are in the audio and when; it does **not** tell me how voices, music or effects feel. I make no claim about mood, timbre, music quality or lip-sync.
- For "without subtitles" I used the sound (as transcribed) plus the picture. The slates that carried the lines in cut-v2 are gone, so unlike last time nothing on screen spells the dialogue out.
- I screened cut-v2 before this one. That memory colours what I notice (e.g. the slates are gone), but I report this cut on its own.

## What I understood as a first-time viewer
Two men, an old, hunched, long-nosed one in an olive coat (Proog) and a young one in a grey top (Emo), travel through an enormous machine of cables, pipes, lifts and glowing halls. Proog is the guide: he insists it is safe, then that it is not, and tells Emo to listen. Emo gets bored, curious and doubtful, and says there is nothing there. They argue, Emo shouts at the machine that it is full of wonders (Hanging Gardens, Colossus), and the machine grows red pipes and takes him. Proog is left kneeling beside Emo's limp body. I followed this and I cared about it. Picture and voices fit together. The two men are easy to tell apart on screen (bald old man in an olive coat and dark red vest, dark-haired young man in a grey top) and they look like the same two people from 0:26 to 9:00.

