- **3:10-3:30** Wide of the lamp over the telephone for about 15 s with little change; "Listen to the sounds of the machine... your breathing" sits on it. Calm, a bit long, but suits the lines.
- **3:33-3:44** Emo with a hand to his chin, then both at a railing, Proog's shoes on carpet. Nice small beats.
- **3:44-4:00 (green hall)** Green brass hall with a horn. Cut into the green machine hall. Beautiful, new colour.
- **4:00-4:30** Proog bounds on pillars across the hall, Emo behind. Cuts here are quick (4:02-4:09 changes several times in 7 s). I did not notice a jump that confused me, but I can only see every 3 s.
- **4:26-4:52** "Don't you ever get tired of this?" ... "clockwork ... ground to a pulp." An explosion at about 4:42 behind them; the two face each other; "Pulp!" at 4:51 is the shouted word: it is audible at the cue time but the recogniser heard "Paul"/"pole", so the word may not read as "pulp". Please judge it by ear.
- **4:52-5:06** About 13 s of an orange lift with very little movement (the least motion of anything in the film). Fine as a breath.
- **5:06-5:40** Proog presses a red button; a spiralling iris/tube; the cage spins; Proog on the lever, face hard. Exciting. Cuts are rapid and I follow them.
- **5:41-5:45** "Emo, close your eyes. Now!" The words and "Now!" are audible; I heard "close ... eyes, now" clearly in the transcript. Picture: Proog's angry close-up with Emo behind.
- **5:52-6:19** Black void, a small platform with both men; Emo looks down, sad. "What do you see at your left side?" / "Nothing." / "And at your right?" / "The same, nothing!" All heard in order; the void looks like nothing, which fits the lines. This is the best-staged scene to me: the picture agrees with what is said.
- **6:19-6:40** Gold-white glowing hall, Emo and Proog small among tubes; 6:25 a flash.
